# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules
#
# Why this file exists:
# Cloudflare Pages by default strips .html and trailing slashes via 308s,
# but DOES NOT redirect the www subdomain to the apex. That left
# www.flotionrecords.com/* serving 200 alongside flotionrecords.com/*,
# which Google Search Console flagged as "Fout met omleiding" because a
# request like http://www.flotionrecords.com/services.html had to chain
# through http→https, www→apex, and .html→extensionless — three hops in
# the worst case.
#
# Rule: every www request goes straight to the canonical apex in ONE
# 301 (permanent) hop, preserving the rest of the URL via :splat.
# The trailing ! makes it a forced rewrite (overrides the default 200
# that Pages would have served for the same path).
https://www.flotionrecords.com/* https://flotionrecords.com/:splat 301!
